<procedure><preliminaryRqmts><reqCondGroup><reqCondDm><reqCond>The used level-temperature gauge is removed.</reqCond><dmRef><dmRefIdent><dmCode modelIdentCode="VH15" systemDiffCode="A" systemCode="10" subSystemCode="0" subSubSystemCode="0" assyCode="00" disassyCode="05" disassyCodeVariant="A" infoCode="520" infoCodeVariant="A" itemLocationCode="A"/></dmRefIdent></dmRef></reqCondDm></reqCondGroup><reqSupportEquips><supportEquipDescrGroup><supportEquipDescr id="seq-0001"><name>Torque wrench, 5 to 50 N·m</name><toolRef toolNumber="TORQUE-WRENCH-50"/><reqQuantity>1</reqQuantity></supportEquipDescr><supportEquipDescr id="seq-0002"><name>Socket, 17 mm</name><toolRef toolNumber="SOCKET-17"/><reqQuantity>1</reqQuantity></supportEquipDescr></supportEquipDescrGroup></reqSupportEquips><reqSupplies><supplyDescrGroup><supplyDescr id="sup-0001"><name>Lint-free cloth</name><supplyRef supplyNumber="LINT-FREE-CLOTH" supplyNumberType="sp05"/><reqQuantity>As required</reqQuantity></supplyDescr><supplyDescr id="sup-0002"><name>Hydraulic oil, HLP 46</name><supplyRef supplyNumber="DIN 51524-2 HLP 46" supplyNumberType="sp02"/><reqQuantity>As required</reqQuantity></supplyDescr></supplyDescrGroup></reqSupplies><reqSpares><spareDescrGroup><spareDescr id="spa-0001"><name>Level-temperature gauge, 127 mm, with seals</name><identNumber><manufacturerCode>VH000</manufacturerCode><partAndSerialNumber><partNumber>VH15-1005</partNumber></partAndSerialNumber></identNumber><reqQuantity>1</reqQuantity></spareDescr></spareDescrGroup></reqSpares><reqSafety><noSafety/></reqSafety></preliminaryRqmts><mainProcedure><proceduralStep><para>Make sure that the part number on the new gauge is VH15-1005.</para></proceduralStep><proceduralStep><para>Put the new seals on the two hollow bolts.</para></proceduralStep><proceduralStep><para>Put the gauge on the tank wall with the thermometer at the bottom. Install the two hollow bolts.</para></proceduralStep><proceduralStep><para>Tighten the hollow bolts to 8 N·m. Do not tighten more: the gauge body can break.</para></proceduralStep><proceduralStep><para>Fill the reservoir to the maximum mark: <dmRef><dmRefIdent><dmCode modelIdentCode="VH15" systemDiffCode="A" systemCode="10" subSystemCode="0" subSubSystemCode="0" assyCode="00" disassyCode="00" disassyCodeVariant="A" infoCode="241" infoCodeVariant="A" itemLocationCode="A"/></dmRefIdent></dmRef>.</para></proceduralStep><proceduralStep><para>Start the unit and let it operate for 5 minutes. Stop the unit and examine the gauge for leaks.</para></proceduralStep></mainProcedure><closeRqmts><reqCondGroup><reqCondNoRef><reqCond>The level-temperature gauge shows the oil level, and there are no leaks.</reqCond></reqCondNoRef></reqCondGroup></closeRqmts></procedure>
